.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt PMC.LOONGARCH 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pmc.loongarch
.Nd LoongArch performance monitoring counters
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libpmc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In pmc.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Xr hwpmc 4
LoongArch backend supports version 1 performance monitoring units with
64-bit counters.
The number of counters is obtained from CPUCFG register 6.
All active CPUs must report compatible PMU parameters.
If these requirements are not met, hardware PMCs are unavailable;
software PMCs described in
.Xr pmc.soft 3
can still be used.
.Pp
The backend supports process-scope and system-scope counting and sampling.
Counter overflow interrupts are delivered through
.Xr cpuic 4 .
Sampling is not precise and may record an instruction address after the
instruction responsible for the event.
.Ss Event Specifiers
The following named events use the Loongson event map.
Their detailed semantics and availability depend on the processor model.
.Bl -column "LOONGARCH-BRANCH_MISSES" "0x00" -offset indent
.It Em Event Ta Em Code
.It Li LOONGARCH-CPU_CYCLES Ta Li 0x00
.It Li LOONGARCH-INSTRUCTIONS Ta Li 0x01
.It Li LOONGARCH-BRANCHES Ta Li 0x02
.It Li LOONGARCH-BRANCH_MISSES Ta Li 0x03
.It Li LOONGARCH-L1I_REFERENCES Ta Li 0x06
.It Li LOONGARCH-L1I_MISSES Ta Li 0x07
.It Li LOONGARCH-L1D_REFERENCES Ta Li 0x08
.It Li LOONGARCH-L1D_MISSES Ta Li 0x09
.It Li LOONGARCH-LL_REFERENCES Ta Li 0x0c
.It Li LOONGARCH-LL_MISSES Ta Li 0x0d
.It Li LOONGARCH-ITLB_MISSES Ta Li 0x3b
.It Li LOONGARCH-DTLB_MISSES Ta Li 0x3c
.El
.Pp
The aliases
.Li cycles ,
.Li instructions ,
.Li instructions-retired ,
.Li branches ,
and
.Li branch-misses
select the corresponding named events.
.Pp
To specify a processor-specific event directly, use
.Li LOONGARCH-RAW,event= Ns Ar code .
The event code is required, may be decimal, hexadecimal, or octal,
and must be in the range 0 through 0x3ff.
The event encoding must be appropriate for the processor being measured.
.Ss Event Qualifiers
Event specifiers accept the following optional comma-separated qualifiers:
.Bl -tag -width "usr"
.It Li os
Count events in kernel privilege level PLV0.
.It Li usr
Count events in user privilege level PLV3.
.El
.Pp
If neither qualifier is specified, both privilege levels are counted.
No edge, invert, threshold, or event-mask qualifiers are supported.
.Ss Sampling
Sampling periods must be positive and no greater than
.Li 0x7fffffffffffffff .
The backend programs overflow at bit 63 of the counter and reloads the
counter after processing an overflow interrupt.
.Ss Examples
Count user-mode retired instructions for a command:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pmcstat -p instructions,usr command
.Ed
.Pp
Sample kernel cycles system-wide:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pmcstat -n 1000000 -S cycles,os
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pmc 3 ,
.Xr pmc.soft 3 ,
.Xr pmc_allocate 3 ,
.Xr pmc_capabilities 3 ,
.Xr cpuic 4 ,
.Xr hwpmc 4 ,
.Xr pmccontrol 8 ,
